 "headline": "deployable fixed integer constants under LOCO: AUROC 0.8411 vs Q1 0.822; BA 0.765 at FRR 5.0% (Q1 BA 0.808 at its own operating point). Per-fold re-selection of weights/tau is WORSE than one fixed constant set (0.776, FRR 14%) - see negative_results.",
 "label_source": "labels/manifest_gold.json human labels (1=good), joined by window id; reasons from caches/perpixel/gold.npz",
 "limitations": "n=150 windows / 7 clips / 50 bad, so every LOCO number has wide clip-bootstrap CIs; a single clip is 6-48 windows (pallet2 has only 6 windows, 2 good), so one resampled clip can move the metric by >0.05. The candidate rule FAMILIES (which physical quantity, which feature) were shortlisted by domain reasoning on this same pool, so a mild selection bias remains even though every threshold, weight and tau is computed on training clips only; the inner-LOCO screen and the outer LOCO share the same 7 clips. Thresholds for 'rel' rules are k x a median measured on training clips, so the deployable Q=4 constant is only as stable as that median (see fold_threshold_stability). Exposure 'abs' constants are physical but were sanity-checked on this pool. The Q1 baseline is cited from the BRIEF, not recomputed in this harness. Nothing here was tuned on the 108-window confirmatory hold-out or on OOD labels.",
