 "negative_results": [
  "PER-FOLD RE-SELECTION OVERFITS: choosing rules/weights/tau separately inside each LOCO fold gives AUROC 0.7764 / BA 0.7100 with FRR 14.0% (budget was 5%), while freezing ONE constant set and only recomputing the measured 'rel' thresholds per fold gives AUROC 0.8411 / BA 0.7650 at FRR 5.0%. With 6 training clips the selection step is noisier than the quantity it selects.",
  "QUALITY VETO IS INERT IN-DOMAIN: no absolute exposure/frozen rule (dark_frac>0.5, bright_frac>0.05, frozen_frac>0.02, over_mean>0.02, under_mean>0.5) entered the top-8 inner-LOCO screen, so the 'weights+veto' variant is numerically identical to 'weights' (0.7764/0.7100). Veto rules are a safety net for OOD, not an in-domain accuracy lever.",
  "LEXICOGRAPHIC/PRIORITY OR IS WEAKER: OR of the top-j rules with j chosen on training clips gives AUROC 0.6650 / BA 0.6650 at FRR 13.0%; a single priority rule cannot use the graded evidence.",
  "P_diff_e_min is identically 0 for all 150 windows -> no information, dropped.",
  "G_dup_hash_mean is identically 0.5 for all 150 windows -> no information, dropped.",
  "G_frozen_frac is 0 for every good window and for 22/23 NO_ACTIVE_WORK windows; its absolute 0.02 veto fires on <=1 window, so the FROZEN_STATIC veto contributes nothing on in-domain data.",
  "Sharpness rules on pp.lap_var_max / full.luma_mean (not selected) separate TOO_DARK only; they trade good-window false rejects for dark-window hits and lost the inner-LOCO screen.",
  "G_skin_frac (HANDS_NOT_VISIBLE proxy) fires on many good windows (median good 0.042 vs bad 0.020) and was too weak to enter the top-8 in most folds: in-domain HANDS_NOT_VISIBLE is not separable by skin area alone."
 ],
